summary:
- topic: Budget Referendum Success
  text: The Board Chair and Superintendent both expressed their gratitude to the voters
    of South Portland for the resounding support of the school budget referendum,
    which passed with a 22% margin.
- topic: Staff Recognition
  text: The board honored the retirement of Kelly Perkins, a long-serving clerk at
    Brown Elementary School. Several board members shared personal anecdotes praising
    her kindness and dedication, noting she was the 'heart and soul' of the school.
- topic: Personnel Action
  text: The board unanimously approved the hiring of Ashley Peterson as a new third-grade
    teacher for Kaler Elementary School.
- topic: SPESPA Agreement
  text: Following an executive session, the board voted unanimously to approve a tentative
    agreement with the South Portland Educational Support Professionals Association
    (SPESPA) regarding an apprentice dispute.
- topic: Interim Superintendent Search
  text: After a second executive session concerning a confidential personnel matter,
    the board voted to engage the Maine School Management Association to begin the
    search for an interim superintendent.
- topic: Leadership Transition Planning
  text: Board members discussed the process for the superintendent transition, emphasizing
    the need for stability and flexibility. They agreed to keep options open for the
    interim's term length to minimize disruption to the district during the school
    year.
- topic: Superintendent Separation Agreement
  text: The board authorized the chair and legal counsel to negotiate a separation
    agreement with Superintendent Matheney, which would be contingent upon the successful
    hiring of an interim superintendent. The final agreement will be made public.
